# TypeScript Code Style

- Prefer clear, descriptive names for variables and functions.
- Annotate exported/public APIs; avoid `any` unless necessary.
- Handle errors first with early returns, avoid deep nesting.
- Derive data rather than relying on implicit side effects.
- Keep comments minimal; only add when clarifying non-obvious behavior.
- Match existing formatting; avoid unrelated refactors in edits.
